    {
      "name": "5 \u2014 Rejections",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "422 \u2014 brand_id is closed",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/manufacturer/gear",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "manufacturer",
                "gear"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              },
              "raw": "{\n  \"items\": [\n    { \"gear_type\": \"webbings\", \"gear_id\": {{gearId}}, \"name\": \"{{gearName}}\", \"changes\": { \"brand_id\": \"17\" } }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "description": "\"webbings has no field(s): brand_id\". One of only two fields we hold that are deliberately closed \u2014 a submitter knows \"Balance Community\", not 17, and an id from a different environment is worse than no answer. Send `brand_name` instead; resolving it to a brand row is the admin's job at patch time. (The other closed field is `classification`.)"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('422', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "422 \u2014 a list of objects",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/manufacturer/gear",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "manufacturer",
                "gear"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              },
              "raw": "{\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"gear_type\": \"webbings\",\n      \"gear_id\": {{gearId}},\n      \"name\": \"{{gearName}}\",\n      \"changes\": { \"material\": [{ \"fiber\": \"Polyester\" }] }\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "description": "A list of scalars is fine (folder 2); a list of objects is not. The store holds prose the admin hand-applies to a *.json file \u2014 there is no sensible rendering of a nested structure, and guessing one would put garbage in the queue."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('422', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "422 \u2014 a typo'd field name",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/manufacturer/gear",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "manufacturer",
                "gear"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              },
              "raw": "{\n  \"items\": [\n    { \"gear_type\": \"webbings\", \"gear_id\": {{gearId}}, \"name\": \"{{gearName}}\", \"changes\": { \"colour\": \"red\" } }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "description": "The real field is `colors`. This guard exists so the admin triage list does not fill with `breaking_stength` and invented fields that no amount of reviewing can turn into a JSON patch."
          },
          "event": [
